{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. You’re here because of nausea and vomiting—can you tell me what happened today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I woke up feeling fine, but right before my big work presentation, I suddenly felt nauseous and started vomiting. I’ve thrown up several times already, all watery, no blood."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fever, abdominal pain, or diarrhea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, none of that. It feels just like my past episodes—probably my gastroparesis flaring up again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. You have type 1 diabetes and a gastric pacer, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, and I’ve had this happen many times before—especially when I’m anxious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. The vomiting likely started because of anxiety, which triggered your gastroparesis. We’ll give you IV fluids and anti-nausea meds to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds good. I haven’t eaten since yesterday—just couldn’t keep anything down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you NPO for now—nothing by mouth—until the vomiting stops. You already got Zofran, Compazine, and Ativan in the ER. How are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little calmer, but still nauseous. The Ativan helped with the anxiety a bit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep monitoring. Your blood sugar was 73 when you arrived—low but not dangerous. We gave insulin and will adjust as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I usually take glargine at night. Should I still take it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll continue your usual 28 units of glargine tonight. We’re also giving sliding scale insulin as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. My blood pressure has been high during these episodes too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your BP was elevated—158/94. That’s considered hypertensive urgency, especially since you couldn’t take your lisinopril today. We’ll restart it once you can keep fluids down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I only take lisinopril 20 mg daily. I’ve never taken metoprolol—I saw it on a past note and got confused."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2199-04-09 15:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Noted. We’ll stick with lisinopril. Your PCP will check your BP after discharge and may adjust the dose if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2199-04-10 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You made it through the night without vomiting. That’s a great sign. Your labs this morning show mild anemia—your hemoglobin dropped from 12.1 to 10.3—but no other major issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2199-04-10 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from the vomiting? I’ve had iron deficiency before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2199-04-10 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely chronic, not acute. We’re not concerned about bleeding—no blood in vomit or stool. We’ll continue monitoring, but no transfusion needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2199-04-10 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief. Can I try drinking something now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2199-04-10 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start with small sips of water. If you keep that down, we’ll advance to clear liquids, then soft foods."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2199-04-10 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my Reglan? I usually take that three times a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2199-04-10 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll restart Reglan once you’re on oral meds. It helps with stomach emptying. We’re also continuing your amitriptyline and citalopram for nerve pain and mood."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2199-04-10 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve kept down water and broth—great job. We’re upgrading you to a soft diet. How’s your nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2199-04-10 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. Still a little anxious, but not nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2199-04-10 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can take your Ativan 0.5 mg as needed for anxiety. We’re also restarting lisinopril and Reglan by mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2199-04-10 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I take Ativan before stressful events to prevent this?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2199-04-10 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s a good idea. The discharge instructions say to take Ativan if you feel anxious and start to feel nauseous—it might stop the cycle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2199-04-11 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had two meals without vomiting—excellent progress. Your blood sugar this morning was 260, a bit high, but expected since you’re not eating normally."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2199-04-11 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll adjust my insulin once I’m back on a regular schedule. No signs of ketoacidosis, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2199-04-11 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct. No ketones, no acidosis. Your sodium is slightly low at 132, but that’s common with vomiting and IV fluids. It should normalize."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2199-04-11 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad it’s not DKA. I’ve been scared of that since I was young."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2199-04-11 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re watching closely. You’re stable now. Planning to discharge you tomorrow morning if you keep doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2199-04-11 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready to go home. What’s the plan for follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2199-04-11 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see your GI doctor tomorrow to discuss your gastric pacer and ongoing gastroparesis. And your PCP next week to check your blood pressure and review lisinopril."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2199-04-12 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had a full night without symptoms. We’ll discharge you home today. All your meds are back to baseline—no changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2199-04-12 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So same doses: glargine 28 units, lisinopril 20 mg, Reglan, citalopram, amitriptyline, and Ativan as needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2199-04-12 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Take Ativan if anxiety starts—might prevent another episode. And call your team if vomiting returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2199-04-12 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll try to manage stress better and follow up as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2199-04-12 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. Stay hydrated, eat small meals, and reach out if you need help. Safe travels home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2199-04-09 15:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2199-04-12 13:14:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes and a history of gastroparesis was admitted for acute nausea and vomiting triggered by anxiety prior to a work presentation. She was kept NPO initially, given IV fluids, and treated with antiemetics including Zofran, Compazine, and Ativan. Her symptoms resolved over 48 hours, and she successfully advanced to a regular diet. Hypertensive urgency was noted on admission, managed by resuming lisinopril. No evidence of DKA or GI bleeding was found. She was discharged home on her baseline medications with instructions to use Ativan as needed for anxiety to prevent vomiting cycles. Follow-up was arranged with GI and PCP for ongoing management.",
    "problems": [
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Persistent vomiting",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Hyposmolality and/or hyponatremia",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified"
    ]
  }
}
